{"path":"io/strstreambuf/~strstreambuf","title":"std::strstreambuf::~strstreambuf","titleHtml":"<span class=\"t-title-prefix\">std::strstreambuf::</span>~strstreambuf","originalUrl":"https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/io/strstreambuf/~strstreambuf","section":"io","kind":"page","summary":"Destroys a std::strstreambuf object. if the object is managing a dynamically-allocated buffer (the buffer state is \"allocated\") and if the object is not frozen, then deallocates the buffer using the deallocation function provided at…","html":"<table class=\"t-dcl-begin\"><tbody>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl t-until-cxx26\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw1\">virtual</span> ~strstreambuf<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\">  </td>\n<td> <span class=\"t-mark\">(deprecated in C++98)</span> <br><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-until-cxx26\">(removed in C++26)</span> </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl-sep\"><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p>Destroys a <code>std::strstreambuf</code> object. if the object is managing a dynamically-allocated buffer (the buffer state is \"allocated\") and if the object is not frozen, then deallocates the buffer using the deallocation function provided at construction or <span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">delete<span class=\"br0\">[</span><span class=\"br0\">]</span></span> if none was provided.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Parameters\">Parameters</h3>\n<p>(none)\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Notes\">Notes</h3>\n<p>This destructor is typically called by the destructor of <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/io/strstream\">std::strstream</a></span>.\n</p><p>If <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/io/strstreambuf/str\">str()</a></span> was called on a dynamic <code>strstream</code> and <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/strstreambuf/freeze\"><code>freeze(false)</code></a> was not called after that, this destructor leaks memory.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Example\">Example</h3>\n<div class=\"t-example\">\n<pre data-lang=\"cpp\"><code><span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;iostream&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;strstream&gt;</span>\n&nbsp;\n<span class=\"kw4\">void</span><span class=\"sy2\">*</span> my_alloc<span class=\"br0\">(</span>size_t n<span class=\"br0\">)</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">{</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/cout\"><span class=\"kw1775\">std::<span class=\"me2\">cout</span></span></a> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">\"my_alloc(\"</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> n <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">\") called<span class=\"es1\">\\n</span>\"</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <span class=\"kw1\">return</span> new <span class=\"kw4\">char</span><span class=\"br0\">[</span>n<span class=\"br0\">]</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">}</span>\n&nbsp;\n<span class=\"kw4\">void</span> my_free<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"kw4\">void</span><span class=\"sy2\">*</span> p<span class=\"br0\">)</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">{</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/cout\"><span class=\"kw1775\">std::<span class=\"me2\">cout</span></span></a> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">\"my_free() called<span class=\"es1\">\\n</span>\"</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    delete<span class=\"br0\">[</span><span class=\"br0\">]</span> <span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"kw4\">char</span><span class=\"sy2\">*</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span>p<span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">}</span>\n&nbsp;\n<span class=\"kw4\">int</span> main<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">{</span>\n    <span class=\"br0\">{</span>\n        <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/strstreambuf\"><span class=\"kw1769\">std::<span class=\"me2\">strstreambuf</span></span></a> buf<span class=\"br0\">(</span>my_alloc, my_free<span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n        <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/basic_ostream\"><span class=\"kw1746\">std::<span class=\"me2\">ostream</span></span></a> s<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span>buf<span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n        s <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"nu16\">1.23</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/manip/ends\"><span class=\"kw1806\">std::<span class=\"me2\">ends</span></span></a><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n        <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/cout\"><span class=\"kw1775\">std::<span class=\"me2\">cout</span></span></a> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> buf.<span class=\"me1\">str</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">'<span class=\"es1\">\\n</span>'</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n        buf.<span class=\"me1\">freeze</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"kw2\">false</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <span class=\"br0\">}</span> <span class=\"co1\">// destructor called here, buffer deallocated</span>\n&nbsp;\n    <span class=\"br0\">{</span>\n        <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/strstreambuf\"><span class=\"kw1769\">std::<span class=\"me2\">strstreambuf</span></span></a> buf<span class=\"br0\">(</span>my_alloc, my_free<span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n        <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/basic_ostream\"><span class=\"kw1746\">std::<span class=\"me2\">ostream</span></span></a> s<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span>buf<span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n        s <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"nu16\">1.23</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/manip/ends\"><span class=\"kw1806\">std::<span class=\"me2\">ends</span></span></a><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n        <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/cout\"><span class=\"kw1775\">std::<span class=\"me2\">cout</span></span></a> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> buf.<span class=\"me1\">str</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">'<span class=\"es1\">\\n</span>'</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n<span class=\"co1\">//      buf.freeze(false);</span>\n    <span class=\"br0\">}</span> <span class=\"co1\">// destructor called here, memory leak!</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">}</span></code></pre>\n<p>Output:\n</p>\n<pre data-output=\"1\"><code>my_alloc(4096) called\n1.23\nmy_free() called\nmy_alloc(4096) called\n1.23</code></pre> \n</div>","headings":[{"depth":3,"text":"Parameters","id":"Parameters"},{"depth":3,"text":"Notes","id":"Notes"},{"depth":3,"text":"Example","id":"Example"}],"breadcrumbs":[{"path":"","title":"C++ reference"},{"path":"io","title":"Input/output library"},{"path":"io/strstreambuf","title":"std::strstreambuf"}],"children":[],"map":{"label":"std::strstreambuf::~strstreambuf","children":[{"label":"Declarations","note":"1 declaration; revisions: until C++26. Destroys a std::strstreambuf object. if the object is managing a dynamically-allocated buffer (the buffer state is…"},{"label":"Parameters","note":"(none)"},{"label":"Notes","note":"This destructor is typically called by the destructor of std::strstream."},{"label":"Example"}]},"standards":["C++26"],"wordCount":175,"codeBlockCount":2}
